// D1784 — `negation-alias-binding.matrix.vl` over a value whose rep is NOT the i32 default.
// A negation names no rep, so the binding takes its initializer's; that was closed for i32,
// boolean and string while every `letIs*` classifier still opened with `if d.letType >= 0 {
// …read the annotation…; return false }`, so an f64 global was check-clean invalid wasm and
// an f64 local a loud refusal.
//
// THE VALUE IS WHY THIS TEMPLATE EXISTS. Its sibling's `@@VALUE@@` is `5`, which shares the
// i32 default and so cannot see a rep disagreement at all — the sibling graded 34 of 44 with
// every f64 cell invisible. A `1.5` here is the whole difference.
//
// NO `type` DECLARATION MAY BE ADDED beyond the negation alias itself: the alias face and the
// inline `!string` face must both be graded, since they resolve to the same arena negation.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
type N = !string
// @@VALUE@@
1.5
// @@TYPE@@
N
// @@PROOF@@
print(v)
// @@WANT@@
1.5
